Package: frostbyte
Version: 1.1.0-1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: VanguardArts <VanguardArts@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: dkms, kmod, python3, python3-pyqt6
Recommends: linux-headers-generic
Homepage: https://github.com/VanguardArts/frostbyte
Description: NitroSense/PredatorSense-style fan & thermal control for Acer laptops
 FrostByte is an open-source replacement for Acer's NitroSense utility on
 Linux: per-fan manual control, MAX mode, custom fan curves, thermal
 profiles with per-power-source memory, battery charge limiter, and a live
 monitoring dashboard (PyQt6 GUI + frostctl CLI).
 .
 Fan speeds and sensors are driven by the vendored acer-wmi-linuwu kernel
 driver, built automatically via DKMS for the running kernel and rebuilt on
 every kernel update. A small daemon owns all hardware access and enforces a
 thermal safety override; the GUI and CLI talk to it over a local socket.
 The dedicated NitroSense "N" key toggles the GUI, as on Windows.
 .
 Developed and tested on the Acer Nitro AN517-54; supports all models
 handled by the acer-wmi-linuwu driver.
